  "conclusion": "corresponds",
  "rationale": "Transfer checks field/name membership and distinct fresh destinations, Bind removes exactly the matched object and prepends all its slots, and Step first evaluates then binds. These are explicitly local-frame rules using the extended syntax, lifted to the public machine by patternOperation and the previously defined GC/exit wrapper. Empty slots transfer as empty bindings; no child object is removed by unpacking itself. The machine/gc/steps units introduce the lifetime notation; inherited syntax, storage and typing notation remain in the listed dependency units. Functions keeps its explicit inherited-machinery forward reference to the appendix.",
